What this notice has and has not been checked against
-----------------------------------------------------

The attributions here cover the dependencies that have been validated against
their published licences: everything compiled into the binaries Forge
distributes, and every source tree vendored into this repository.

Cargo.lock also resolves crates for targets Forge does not currently build —
Android, WebAssembly, Redox, and other platform-specific graphs. Those have not
been checked one by one. Windows is no longer among them, though what CI
establishes there is narrower than the rest: the protocol, search engine and
terminal client run their full suites on every push to main and on pull
requests; the agent builds and runs its provider-fault matrix, not its unit
tests; and the editor's Windows build is marked informational and does not gate,
because no runner had ever attempted it. The editor has been built and tested
there by hand — see FAILURE-TESTING.md. So the Windows graph is linked into
something a person can run, even though no signed Windows artifact is published
here and CI alone would not prove it. None of them is linked into anything
distributed here, and they are conventionally MIT or Apache-2.0, but this
notice does not assert that, because nobody has confirmed it yet. Checking the
remainder is outstanding work, and the intention is that this section
eventually describes an empty set.

If you are relying on this notice for a compliance review, that is the boundary
of what it currently claims.


